{
  "id": "product-of-array-except-self",
  "title": "Product of Array Except Self",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "categories": ["array", "prefix-sum"],
  "descriptionMd": "Given an integer array `nums`, build an array `answer` where `answer[i]` is the product of **every element of `nums` except `nums[i]`**.\n\nYou are **not allowed to use division**, and your solution should run in O(n) time. The arrays may contain zeros and negative numbers; every product is guaranteed to fit in a 32-bit signed integer.\n\n**Example 1**\n\n```\nnums = [1, 2, 3, 4]\n→ [24, 12, 8, 6]\n```\nFor index 1, the product of the other elements is `1 · 3 · 4 = 12`.\n\n**Example 2**\n\n```\nnums = [-1, 1, 0, -3, 3]\n→ [0, 0, 9, 0, 0]\n```\nOnly position 2 skips the zero, so it is the only non-zero result.\n\n**Follow-up:** can you do it using only O(1) extra space besides the output array?",
  "constraints": ["2 ≤ nums.length ≤ 10⁵", "-30 ≤ nums[i] ≤ 30", "Every product of a prefix or suffix of `nums` fits in a 32-bit signed integer."],
  "hints": ["The value at index i is (product of everything to its left) × (product of everything to its right).", "Can you compute all the \"left products\" in one pass and all the \"right products\" in another?", "The output array itself can hold the left products, and a single running variable can supply the right products."],
  "signature": {
    "functionName": "productExceptSelf",
    "params": [{ "name": "nums", "type": "int[]" }],
    "returns": "int[]"
  },
  "comparator": "exact",
  "tests": [
